### P4 – Tuning Challenge

The module includes:
- Randomly generated first-order plants with hidden parameters.
- Interactive Kp, Ki, and Kd adjustments.
- Closed-loop simulation using Euler integration.
- Overshoot, settling time, and steady-state error calculations.
- Pass/fail checks and a scoring system.
- Open-loop testing and a Predict, then Check activity.

### My System – Micromouse PID Control

Our Micromouse project uses a GA12-N20 DC gear motor with an encoder, an ESP32 development board, and a DRV8833 motor driver.

The page includes:
- A first-order motor model.
- Interactive PID tuning and response simulation.
- Performance measurements and control signal visualization.
- ESP32 Arduino code generation.

**Note:** The hardware has not arrived yet. The current simulation uses assumed plant parameters (K = 500 RPM per normalized PWM input and τ = 0.25 s). These are not experimentally measured values. The model and controller will need validation after physical testing.

